<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111324" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλο-μόχθηρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>loving bad men,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philonid.
				13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>loving evil,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eustr.
				<u>in EN</u>
				16.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>fond of toil</i> or <i>labour,</i>
			
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλόθηρος</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				535d
			</span></i> (ap.<i><span class="en">
				Stob.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
